title: SIDEEYE Backdoor C2 Beacon to PeopleSoft Exploitation Server
id: 9ba88d25-72f4-4380-aa2e-17da1ef482e7
status: experimental
description: Detects network connections to 162.219.30.165 over TCP 3333 and 3334, the C2 used by the SIDEEYE backdoor delivered through Oracle PeopleSoft PeopleTools exploitation (CVE-2026-35273) alongside Neo-reGeorg tunnels and MeshCentral agents in the UNC6240/ShinyHunters-related campaign.
references:
  - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/shinyhunters-renewed-mass-exploitation-campaign-targeting-oracle-peoplesoft
  - https://www.reuters.com/world/shinyhunters-hackers-say-they-breached-federal-bureau-investigation-no-immediate-2026-09-22/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-30
tags:
  - attack.initial-access
  - attack.persistence
  - attack.stealth
  - attack.command-and-control
  - attack.t1190
  - attack.t1505
  - attack.t1116
  - attack.t1572
  - attack.t1219
logsource:
  category: network_connection
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_c2:
    DestinationIp: '162.219.30.165'
    DestinationPort:
      - 3333
      - 3334
  condition: selection_c2
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely; the address has no legitimate business use, but shared hosting or sinkholing could reuse it
level: high

